{
 "_doc": "fo. foley for the Down With Hunger explainer: one kitchen/desk palette (wood knocks, rubber stamps on paper, mouth/cork pops, a fridge door, a steel pot and cutlery, glass jars on a wooden shelf, pencil on paper, sticky notes). Every sample is a real CC0 recording from audio/assets/manifests/foley.json (no Mixkit, no CC BY). Point sources are mono, centred (pan 0 or cue pan scaled to +-0.15). Most effects sit under continuous narration, so most are high-passed (no rumble) and get a 2-4 kHz dip; levels are set by rule gain_db on peak-normalised samples. Runs are thinned by id regex (the bubble run, the jar ticks).",
